# "Whenever enchanted creature attacks or blocks, attach any number of target Equipment you control to it": Bot1's
# enchanted Ornithopter blocks Bot2's attacking Ornithopter on turn 4. Bot2's own Skullclamp is refused as a target (it is
# not an Equipment Bot1 controls) beside Bot1's Skullclamp, the positive control; Bot1 chooses just that one of its two
# Equipment ("any number" is not "all"), so Lightning Greaves stays unattached. The blocker is then 3/3 with first
# strike and kills the 0/2 attacker before it deals damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Super-Soldier Serum
Skullclamp
Lightning Greaves
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Skullclamp
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Super-Soldier Serum.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Skullclamp.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Skullclamp.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Greaves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
Bot1.Block(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter > Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Skullclamp)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Skullclamp.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Lightning Greaves.AttachedTo = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp.AttachedTo = (absent)
